message.content:
{
  "summary": "This bill would change how the office of the comptroller of the treasury reviews and reports on foundational literacy skills plans. The comptroller would be required to review plans submitted to the department for approval to ensure they meet specific requirements and state board rules. This review must examine whether the department initially approved or denied the plans and any required revisions. These findings must be included in the comptroller's reports.\n\nAdditionally, the bill would require the comptroller to review data, practices, and outcomes related to this part of the law, with the department of education providing requested information as soon as practicable. Every three years, the comptroller must publish a report of these findings on its website and submit it to the state board of education and the chairs of the relevant senate and house committees. The act would take effect as soon as it becomes law."
}
